input has spaces between numbers; our read_int will skip non-digit characters automatically.\n\nNow integral image construction:\n\nstd::vector<long long> II((n+1)*(n+1), 0);\nfor (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n    long long row_sum = 0;\n    int base_curr = (i+1)*(n+1); // index of start of current row in II\n    int base_prev = i*(n+1);\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n        int val = read_int();\n        row_sum += val;\n        II[base_curr + j + 1] = II[base_prev + j + 1] + row_sum;\n    }\n}\n\nThis computes II correctly: for each cell (i+1, j+1), it adds the horizontal prefix sum of current row to the vertical accumulation from previous rows.\n\nWe don't need mat or H vectors. This reduces memory footprint and improves cache usage.\n\nNow search loop with 2D tiling:\n\nint mxSum = -2147483648;\nconst int B = 32; // block size\nfor (int ii = 0; ii <= n-s; ii += B) {\n    int i_end = std::min(ii + B, n - s + 1);\n    for (int jj = 0; jj <= n-s; jj += B) {\n        int j_end = std::min(jj + B, n - s + 1);\n        // Precompute? Not needed.\n        #pragma ivdep\n        for (int i = ii; i < i_end; ++i) {\n            long long *row_i = &II[i*(n+1)];\n            long long *row_is = &II[(i+s)*(n+1)];\n            for (int j = jj; j < j_end; ++j) {\n                long long sub_sum = row_is[j+s] - row_i[j+s] - row_is[j] + row_i[j];\n                if (sub_sum > mxSum)\n                    mxSum = static_cast<int>(sub_sum);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nWe use restrict pointers? We can declare local pointers as __restrict__ to help compiler. But the vector data is accessed through multiple pointers; we can add:\n\nlong long * __restrict__ II_ptr = II.data();\n\nBut careful: II_ptr may alias with other pointers if not used carefully. Since we only access via this pointer, it's fine.\n\nWe'll also add #pragma GCC ivdep or #pragma ivdep (Intel). We'll use #pragma ivdep as that is supported by both gcc and icc? Actually gcc supports #pragma GCC ivdep sinc